# Wave I.8 — Manifest-synced admin host product deps

## Problem

Wave I.7 classified products into `devDependencies` and required admin-transpile completeness, but `apps/web/package.json` product keys were still a **hand list**. Evidence:

- `@app-tour/workspace-finance-ws4` was declared though **no** web codegen/plugin loader imports it (orphan relative to product trunk).
- Adding a product trunk workspace required editing `package.json` by hand (same dual-SoT class as pre–C.c guest-runtime).

Guest-runtime already rewrites product deps from manifests (`syncGuestWorkspaceRuntimePackageJson`). Admin web did not.

## Decision

1. Product set for web = `productWorkspaceManifests(manifests).map(m => m.package)` (same trunk as plugin loaders / boundary allowlist — excludes `registryOnly` finance/booking fixtures).
2. Codegen owns **only** those `@app-tour/workspace-*` product keys (not sdk):
   - Must live in **`devDependencies`** as `workspace:*`
   - Must **not** appear in `dependencies` / `optionalDependencies`
   - Exact set match — extras removed, missing added
3. `pnpm run generate:workspace-registry` syncs; `--check` fails on drift.
4. `guard:host-workspace-deps` calls the same verify for web (classification + exact product trunk).

## Out of scope

- `optionalDependencies` / IgnorePlugin removal
- Syncing `apps/api` product deps (different load story)
- Expanding admin `transpilePackages` to the full product trunk (theme/stylesheet gate stays)

## Status

**DONE** — sync + check wired; finance-ws4 hand dep dropped by sync.

## Verify

```bash
pnpm run generate:workspace-registry
pnpm run generate:workspace-registry -- --check
pnpm run guard:host-workspace-deps
pnpm run wave-i0:guard
node --test scripts/test/admin-web-product-deps.spec.mjs
pnpm --filter @apps/web exec node --import tsx --test \
  test/wave-i-7-host-install-classification.spec.ts \
  test/wave-i-8-admin-web-product-deps.spec.ts
```
